{% doc %}
  Emits the canonical Prince Tires locations data as a JSON island that
  client-side code (the booking modals, the contact map) reads. The values are
  derived from pt-nap (the single Liquid source) via its `field: 'json'` mode, so
  the JSON the browser sees can never drift from what the page server-renders.

  Booking surfaces send the location `slug` ('sw' | 'ne') as the location id to
  /api/availability and /api/book; the app resolves slug -> location.

  Render ONCE per page (the booking snippets/layout include it). Reading it in JS:
    const LOCATIONS = JSON.parse(document.getElementById('pt-locations-data').textContent);

  @example
  {% render 'pt-locations' %}
{% enddoc %}

<script id="pt-locations-data" type="application/json">
[
  {% render 'pt-nap', location: 'sw', field: 'json' %},
  {% render 'pt-nap', location: 'ne', field: 'json' %}
]
</script>
